---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Implementation, Onboarding & Enablement" current="/implementation-enablement/" description="Richard Allen's transferable experience in software migrations, onboarding, training, release support, documentation, system transitions, and enablement.">
<section class="role-hero impl-hero"><div class="container role-hero-grid">
  <div class="role-hero-copy">
    <div class="eyebrow light">Implementation, Onboarding & Enablement</div>
    <h1>Make change understandable before asking people to adopt it.</h1>
    <p>My experience is strongest where implementation connects customers, support teams, documentation, training, software change, systems transitions, testing, and day-to-day adoption.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button button-light" href="/case-studies/">See implementation case studies</a><a class="role-hero-link" href="/resume/">View résumé →</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="migration-panel" aria-label="Hosted service migration from Kotter-hosted HawkSoft Online to a Portland-area replacement provider, moving hundreds of agencies and finishing at least one month ahead of deadline">
    <div class="migration-title">MAJOR HOSTED-SERVICE MIGRATION</div>
    <div class="migration-map">
      <div class="host legacy-host"><span>LEGACY</span><strong>Kotter-hosted<br/>HawkSoft Online</strong></div>
      <div class="move-lane"><div class="agency-dots" aria-hidden="true">{Array.from({length:14}).map(() => <i></i>)}</div><div class="move-line"><span></span></div><strong>Hundreds</strong><small>of insurance agencies</small></div>
      <div class="host new-host"><span>REPLACEMENT</span><strong>Portland-area<br/>hosted provider</strong><b>1+ month early</b></div>
    </div>
    <div class="migration-footer"><span>customer communication</span><i>+</i><span>technical coordination</span><i>+</i><span>support continuity</span></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="impl-proof-band"><div class="container impl-proof-grid">
  <div><strong>Hundreds</strong><span>of agencies moved in the major hosted-service transition</span></div>
  <div><strong>1+ month</strong><span>ahead of the critical migration deadline</span></div>
  <div><strong>6 months</strong><span>advance communication for a major accounting-software redesign</span></div>
  <div><strong>Biweekly</strong><span>developer/staff education during the final two months</span></div>
</div></section>

<section class="section readiness-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Change runway</div><h2>Implementation starts before go-live—and continues after it.</h2></div><p class="section-note">A major HawkSoft accounting-software redesign was treated as a readiness program, not a launch-day announcement.</p></div>
  <div class="readiness-runway" aria-label="Six-month software change readiness timeline">
    <div class="runway-step prepare"><span>6 MONTHS OUT</span><strong>Prepare</strong><small>Advance communication begins; set expectations and surface learning needs.</small></div>
    <div class="runway-line"><i></i></div>
    <div class="runway-step educate"><span>FINAL 2 MONTHS</span><strong>Educate</strong><small>Biweekly developer/staff education, training creation, and recurring coordination.</small></div>
    <div class="runway-line"><i></i></div>
    <div class="runway-step launch"><span>GO-LIVE</span><strong>Launch</strong><small>Extra coverage, troubleshooting, and rapid practical guidance.</small></div>
    <div class="runway-line"><i></i></div>
    <div class="runway-step reinforce"><span>AFTER LAUNCH</span><strong>Reinforce</strong><small>Continued training and support as new workflows became normal work.</small></div>
  </div>
  <div class="testing-strip"><div><span>BUILD VALIDATION</span><strong>Test the change before teaching the change.</strong></div><p>At The Kotter Group, performed broad functional run-throughs of new software builds, reproduced problems, documented expected-versus-actual behavior, identified usability issues, and created product/training material around the resulting features and workflows.</p></div>
</div></section>

<section class="section impl-evidence-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Change made usable</div><h2>Migration, readiness, training, testing, and adoption.</h2></div><p class="section-note">Different systems, same goal: help people understand and successfully use the new way of working.</p></div>
  <div class="grid two value-grid impl-card-grid">
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">MOVE</div><h3>Hosted-service migration</h3><p>Project-managed and coordinated a major HawkSoft Online hosting transition that moved hundreds of insurance agencies from the Kotter-hosted environment to a Portland-area replacement provider. The migration finished at least one month ahead of the critical deadline while customer communication, support, and technical coordination stayed connected.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">GO</div><h3>Major software release support</h3><p>Led staff readiness for a significant HawkSoft accounting-software redesign through six months of advance communication, biweekly developer/staff education during the final two months, extra launch coverage, and continued training afterward. Historical interview records support Richard’s role in creating and participating in training and related meetings for the change.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">TRAIN</div><h3>Training & enablement</h3><p>Trained customers and staff on software workflows, troubleshooting, product changes, features, and best practices; also created training documentation, presentations, webinars, onboarding materials, SOPs, and customer-facing instructions.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">TEST</div><h3>Product, procedure & functional testing</h3><p>At The Kotter Group, created product and training documentation, presentations, webinars, online content, customer communications, and procedure material. For new software builds, performed broad functional run-throughs to confirm expected behavior and identify breakage before supporting documentation and education.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">BILL</div><h3>Billing-system transition</h3><p>At Willamette Broadband, supported the move to a new billing system while continuing customer service, billing, scheduling, troubleshooting, complaint resolution, and customer training.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">SCAN</div><h3>DOS replacement & X-ray digitization</h3><p>At Shady Grove Adventist Hospital, helped implement a new tracking system replacing a DOS-based process and helped create the procedures used to digitize thousands of X-ray films. The transition improved efficiency by approximately 30%.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section tight"><div class="container"><div class="scope-banner"><strong>Scope</strong><span>Source-supported migration coordination · release support · functional testing · training · documentation · onboarding · systems change</span><small>This does not claim formal UAT ownership, product-roadmap ownership, or a dedicated Implementation Manager title.</small></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/case-studies/">See case studies</a><a class="button secondary" href="/resume/">View résumé</a><a class="button secondary" href="/contact/">Contact</a></div></div></section>

<style>
  .role-hero{padding:4.8rem 0 4rem;color:#fff;overflow:hidden}.impl-hero{background:radial-gradient(circle at 84% 18%,rgba(107,91,181,.36),transparent 28%),linear-gradient(128deg,#102f55 0%,#153e75 52%,#5a4f8a 100%)}.role-hero-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(420px,1fr);gap:3rem;align-items:center}.role-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.8rem,6vw,5rem);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.05em;margin:.7rem 0 1.25rem}.role-hero p{font-size:1.15rem;color:#e7edf5;max-width:720px}.role-hero-link{color:#fff;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;align-self:center}.migration-panel{padding:1.2rem;border-radius:24px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.08);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18);box-shadow:0 24px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.2)}.migration-title{font-size:.72rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.15em;color:#ded6ff;margin:.2rem 0 1rem}.migration-map{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.2fr 1fr;gap:.7rem;align-items:center}.host{min-height:160px;padding:1rem;border-radius:17px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.08);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.13);display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;text-align:center}.host span{font-size:.67rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#d8e0eb}.host strong{font-size:1rem;line-height:1.3;margin:.4rem 0}.new-host b{display:inline-block;align-self:center;margin-top:.4rem;padding:.28rem .55rem;border-radius:999px;background:#e9f7f5;color:#0f766e;font-size:.72rem}.move-lane{text-align:center}.agency-dots{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(7,8px);gap:5px;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.65rem}.agency-dots i{width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#cabfff}.move-line{height:3px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.18);position:relative;margin:.5rem}.move-line span{position:absolute;right:0;top:-4px;border-left:8px solid #d7ccff;border-top:5px solid transparent;border-bottom:5px solid transparent}.move-lane strong{display:block;font-size:1.4rem;color:#e5ddff}.move-lane small{color:#dce4ee}.migration-footer{display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:.9rem;color:#dce6ef;font-size:.74rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em}.migration-footer i{font-style:normal;color:#aaa0d7}.impl-proof-band{background:#fff;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.impl-proof-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr)}.impl-proof-grid>div{padding:1.35rem;border-right:1px solid var(--border)}.impl-proof-grid>div:last-child{border-right:0}.impl-proof-grid strong{display:block;font-size:1.9rem;line-height:1;color:var(--violet)}.impl-proof-grid span{display:block;margin-top:.4rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.35}.readiness-section{background:linear-gradient(180deg,#f7f5ff,#fff)}.readiness-runway{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr .4fr 1fr .4fr 1fr .4fr 1fr;align-items:center}.runway-step{min-height:180px;padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;background:#fff;box-shadow:0 10px 28px rgba(23,32,42,.05)}.runway-step span{display:block;font-size:.67rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.11em;color:var(--violet)}.runway-step strong{display:block;font-size:1.08rem;margin:.45rem 0}.runway-step small{color:var(--muted);line-height:1.4}.runway-line{height:4px;background:#ded7f5;position:relative}.runway-line i{position:absolute;right:-2px;top:-4px;border-left:7px solid var(--violet);border-top:6px solid transparent;border-bottom:6px solid transparent}.prepare{border-top:4px solid var(--accent-2)}.educate{border-top:4px solid var(--gold)}.launch{border-top:4px solid var(--violet)}.reinforce{border-top:4px solid var(--teal)}.testing-strip{margin-top:1.2rem;padding:1.35rem;border-radius:20px;background:linear-gradient(110deg,#4b3e76,#6b5bb5);color:#fff;display:grid;grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;gap:1.5rem;align-items:center}.testing-strip span{display:block;font-size:.7rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#ded6ff}.testing-strip strong{display:block;font-size:1.3rem;line-height:1.2;margin-top:.2rem}.testing-strip p{margin:0;color:#f1effb}.impl-evidence-section{background:#fff}.impl-card-grid .card{transition:transform .18s ease,box-shadow .18s ease}.impl-card-grid .card:hover{transform:translateY(-3px);box-shadow:0 15px 35px rgba(23,32,42,.08)}.scope-banner{display:grid;gap:.35rem;padding:1.2rem 1.3rem;border-radius:18px;background:var(--violet-soft);border-left:5px solid var(--violet)}.scope-banner strong{font-size:1.1rem}.scope-banner small{color:var(--muted)}
  @media(max-width:1000px){.role-hero-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.readiness-runway{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.7rem}.runway-line{display:none}.testing-strip{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  @media(max-width:800px){.impl-proof-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.migration-map{grid-template-columns:1fr}.move-line{width:4px;height:40px;margin:.4rem auto}.move-line span{right:-4px;top:auto;bottom:-2px;border-left:6px solid transparent;border-right:6px solid transparent;border-top:8px solid #d7ccff;border-bottom:0}.agency-dots{grid-template-columns:repeat(7,8px)}}
  @media(max-width:600px){.role-hero{padding:3.4rem 0}.role-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.5rem,12vw,3.8rem)}.impl-proof-grid,.readiness-runway{grid-template-columns:1fr}.impl-proof-grid>div{border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.impl-proof-grid>div:last-child{border-bottom:0}}
  @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.impl-card-grid .card{transition:none}.impl-card-grid .card:hover{transform:none}}
</style>
</BaseLayout>
